  'ctx.nestedMills': 'A ring mill returns ${v}$ watts. A stand carries {a} mills. There are {b} stands along the scarp, all of them turning.',
  'ctx.nestedBuoys': 'A sounding buoy pings for ${v}$ seconds a cycle. A string carries {a} buoys. {b} strings are moored across the channel.',
  'ctx.claimStencil': 'The stencil kit in the paint locker has its letters numbered so nobody loses one, and Cadet {who} has read {pos} straight off it. The manifest reads ${v} = {val}$.',
  'ctx.claimTeacher': 'Cadet {who} is certain, because somebody who was certain told them, that ${v}$ comes to {pos}. Certainty is not a source. The manifest is, and it says ${v} = {val}$.',
  'ctx.claimSpine': 'The spine of the training manual numbers every letter of the alphabet, for indexing. Cadet {who} has read that as a value and written {pos}. The manifest says ${v} = {val}$.',
  'ctx.claimQuiz': 'The quiz answer sheet from last term has {pos} against ${v}$, because last term the question was about the alphabet. This one is not. The manifest says ${v} = {val}$.',
  'ctx.claimKeel': 'Somebody painted a numbered alphabet along the keel walk decades ago, and Cadet {who} has walked it as far as {pos}. The manifest reads ${v} = {val}$.',
  'ctx.claimMate': 'Cadet {who} will tell you, without being asked, that ${v}$ is {pos} because ${v}$ is letter number {pos}, and will tell you again later. The manifest says ${v} = {val}$ both times.',
  'ctx.logBellows': 'The bellows log derives every line from the rule written across the head of the column. One line came back scorched off.',
  'ctx.logCrusher': 'The crusher does not weigh its output, it computes it, from one rule at the top of the column. A jam took one line out of the middle.',
  'ctx.logSluice': 'The sluice log carries the rule it was computed from at the head of the column. A surge lifted one reading clean off the board.',
  'ctx.logAviary': 'The aviary count is a computation, not a count: one rule above the column, every line below it obeying. One line was lost to the storm.',
  'ctx.logCompass': 'The compass table applies one rule to every heading it is given, and prints that rule over the column. One heading has nothing written beside it.',
  'ctx.logGrinder': 'The grinder log states its rule at the head of the column and every pass below was worked out that way. One pass lost its figure.',
  'ctx.logStack': 'The stack gauge computes each entry from the rule at the head of the column. Soot took one entry and left the rest legible.',
  'ctx.logWeir': 'The weir log writes the rule it uses above the column and applies it to every reading. One reading was carried away.',
  'ctx.logDrier': 'The drier log derives every row from one rule, printed where a header belongs. One row came back blank.',
  'ctx.logCarding': 'The carding log is one rule at the top and a line for every batch that went through. One batch has no number against it.',
  'ctx.logHone': 'A honing log pairs the setting it was given with the finish it returned. One line kept the finish and lost the setting.',
  'ctx.logBleach': 'The bleach log records the strength that went into the vat and the strength that came out. One line lost what went in.',
  'ctx.rooftank': 'A roof tank starts the day at {b} and loses {a} for every minute the sun is straight on the lid.',
  'ctx.creditLine': 'A survey account opens at {b} credits and the ring takes {a} for every minute the array is pointed anywhere useful.',
  'ctx.snowPack': 'The pack stands at {b} and gives up {a} for every minute the thaw wind runs across it.',
  'ctx.brakeShoe': 'A brake shoe starts the descent at {b} and wears {a} off for every minute the drum is turning under it.',
  'ctx.tideRace': 'The race is running at {b} and drops {a} for every minute past the turn.',
  'ctx.kilnHeat': 'The kiln comes off full heat at {b} and loses {a} for every minute the doors are open.',
  'ctx.tramChart': 'A tram has been climbing the scarp at one steady rate all morning, and the chart has the whole climb.',
  'ctx.pumpChart': 'The pump has drawn the level down at one rate since it started, and somebody charted every minute of it.',
  'ctx.mothChart': 'A survey moth has been running the coast at one pace since the light, and the plotter drew all of it.',
